        skos:exactMatch  obo:CHEBI_74856;
        skos:note        "An inorganic chloride salt with formula SbCl<small><sub>3</sub></small>. It is used as a reagent for detecting vitamin A and related carotenoids, reacting with the carotenoid to form a blue complex that can be measured by colorimetry (the Carr-Price test). Solutions of antimony trichloride were formerly used for dissolving and removing horn stubs from calves and goats."@en .

