        skos:exactMatch  obo:CHEBI_37249 , obo:CHEBI_22977;
        skos:note        "An element in the zinc group of the periodic table with atomic number 48, atomic mass 112, M.P. 321°C, and B.P. 765°C). An odourless, tasteless, and highly poisonous soft, ductile, lustrous metal with electropositive properties. It has eight stable isotopes: <small><sup>106</small></sup>Cd, <small><sup>108</small></sup>Cd,<small><sup> 110</small></sup>Cd, <small><sup>111</small></sup>Cd, <small><sup>112</small></sup>Cd, <small><sup>113</small></sup>Cd, <small><sup>114</small></sup>Cd and <small><sup>116</small></sup>Cd, with <small><sup>112</small></sup>Cd and <small><sup>114</small></sup>Cd being the most common."@en .

