obo:CHEBI_81526  rdf:type           owl:Class;
        rdfs:label                  "endrin";
        rdfs:subClassOf             obo:CHEBI_25705 , obo:CHEBI_32955;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf             [] ;
        obo:IAO_0000115             "An organochlorine compound resulting from the epoxidation of the double bond of isodrin. It is the <em>endo</em>, <em>endo</em> stereoisomer of dieldrin. It is an insecticide mainly used on field crops such as cotton and grains and has also been used as a rodenticide to control mice and voles. The product is banned in many countries since it is a persistent organic pollutant.";
